      "text": "To determine the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we need to understand the periodicity of the individual trigonometric functions involved and then find their common period.\n\n1. **Period of \\(\\tan x\\):**\n   The function \\(\\tan x\\) has a periodicity of \\(\\pi\\). This means:\n   \\[\n   \\tan(x + \\pi) = \\tan x\n   \\]\n\n2. **Period of \\(\\cot x\\):**\n   The function \\(\\cot x\\) also has a periodicity of \\(\\pi\\). This means:\n   \\[\n   \\cot(x + \\pi) = \\cot x\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combined Period:**\n   Since both \\(\\tan x\\) and \\(\\cot x\\) have a period of \\(\\pi\\), the expression \\( \\tan x + \\cot x \\) will repeat its values every \\(\\pi\\) units. Therefore, the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\(\\pi\\).\n\nThus, the period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\pi}\\).",
