      "text": "To find the period of the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\), we need to determine the smallest positive value \\( T \\) such that \\( y(x + T) = y(x) \\) for all \\( x \\).\n\nFirst, recall the periodicity and symmetry properties of the tangent and cotangent functions. The tangent function \\( \\tan x \\) has a period of \\( \\pi \\), and the cotangent function \\( \\cot x \\) also has a period of \\( \\pi \\). Therefore, \\( \\tan(x + \\pi) = \\tan x \\) and \\( \\cot(x + \\pi) = \\cot x \\).\n\nNow, let's consider the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\). We need to check if adding any integer multiple of \\( \\pi \\) to \\( x \\) keeps the function unchanged:\n\\[ y(x + \\pi) = \\tan(x + \\pi) + \\cot(x + \\pi) = \\tan x + \\cot x = y(x). \\]\n\nThis shows that the function \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is periodic with period \\( \\pi \\). To confirm that \\( \\pi \\) is the smallest period, we need to check that no smaller positive number works. Since the tangent and cotangent functions repeat their values every \\( \\pi \\) and these functions are defined over every \\( \\pi \\)-interval, \\( \\pi \\) is indeed the smallest period.\n\nTherefore, the period of \\( y = \\tan x + \\cot x \\) is \\(\\boxed{\\pi}\\).",
